course: dictionary
lesson: 5677
title: Loam, the best soil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe things you can see and touch, like soil in a garden. When you meet loam, read the words around it. «Soils differ: sandy soil has big grains with big gaps, so water drains through it fast.» Then the writer names loam, and you can compare the two.
explain: Loam is rich, dark soil made of a good mix of sand, silt and clay, with rotting plants in it. The sentences call the rotting plants humus. Loam is not just one kind of soil, so it is not too sandy and not too sticky.
explain: «Loam is a mix of sand, silt, clay and humus and is good for most plants.» The clues are a mix and good for most plants, so loam is a balanced soil that helps things grow. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: rich, dark soil that is good for most plants still makes sense.
fact: Loam is rich, dark soil that is very good for growing things.
fact: Loam is a mix of sand, silt and clay, with rotting plants (humus) in it.
fact: Loam holds water but also drains well, so plants get water without going soggy.
fact: Clay soil has tiny grains packed close, so it can become sticky and waterlogged.
fact: In science and gardening lessons you may meet «loamy soil» and «rich loam».
exercise: «Loam is a mix of sand, silt, clay and humus and is good for most plants.» What is loam? | A kind of hard grey rock | *Rich, dark soil that is good for most plants | A type of cloud | A sticky metal used to make pots
exercise: «Soils differ: sandy soil drains fast, and clay holds water and becomes sticky.» Which soil is a balanced mix that is best for farming? | Pebbles | Clay | Sand | *Loam
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Loam is a mix of sand, silt, clay and humus and is good for most plants.» that means rotted plant matter. | sand | silt | *humus | plants
test: Why is loam better for crops than clay? | Clay is rich, dark soil full of rotting plants | Loam is a kind of stone | *Loam holds water and drains well, while clay can become sticky and waterlogged | Sand drains so well that plants never need water
test: What does «rich loam» mean? | A type of gardening tool | Dry, grey dust | *Rich, dark soil made of sand, silt and clay | A small lake
exam: Which phrase is used in science and gardening lessons for soil that is mostly loam? | *Loamy soil | Stony path | Sandy soil | Clay pot
